WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.850 --> 00:00:03.803
What if all the bees on Earth disappeared?

2
00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:09.267
Each visit carries pollen from flower to flower. That’s how many fruits begin.

3
00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:15.089
Without bees, the orchards would go quiet, with less and less fruit each season.

4
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:21.672
About three in four of our main food crops get some help from animal pollinators.

5
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:27.400
But wheat, rice and corn don’t need them. Wind, or the plant itself, does the job.

6
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:32.577
So no, we wouldn’t all die in four years. That quote isn’t even Einstein’s.

7
00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:39.154
Flies, butterflies, birds and bats would still help. But our food would be less varied, and pricier.

8
00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:44.287
So next time a bee drifts past, let it work. It’s carrying your fruit bowl.
